Patch from MiniMyth2 project

Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>



From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: amvdec: T7: byte-swap MPEG-2 output

The stateless MPEG-2 path builds its canvases through
meson_amvdec_canvas_nv12m_spec(), bypassing the T7 shadow frames, so its
CAPTURE buffers came out byte-reversed per 64 bits.

On dos_canvas platforms give each CAPTURE buffer a private frame keyed by
its index (destination and references keep the decoder-native layout) and
swap it into the CAPTURE buffer when a picture, or the first field of a
pair, completes. Other SoCs are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_helpers.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/amvdec_helpers.c
@@ -698,9 +698,21 @@
 int meson_amvdec_canvas_nv12m_spec(struct amvdec_session *sess, struct vb2_buffer *vb,
 			     u32 width, u32 height, u32 *spec)
 {
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Codecs that name destination and references per picture key the
+	 * private frame (see meson_amvdec_shadow_to_capture()) by CAPTURE index.
+	 */
+	if (amvdec_has_dos_canvas(sess->core)) {
+		ret = amvdec_shadow_prepare(sess, vb->index, vb);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	return meson_amvdec_canvas_nv12_spec(sess,
-					     vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(vb, 0),
-					     vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(vb, 1),
+					     amvdec_canvas_plane_addr(sess, vb, vb->index, 0),
+					     amvdec_canvas_plane_addr(sess, vb, vb->index, 1),
 					     width, height, spec);
 }
 
--- a/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_mpeg12.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/amlogic/amvdec/codec_mpeg12.c
@@ -428,6 +428,8 @@
 		m->pair_dst = sess->request_job.dst->vb2_buf.index;
 		m->pair_structure = m->cur_structure;
 		m->pair_temporal_ref = m->cur_temporal_ref;
+		meson_amvdec_shadow_to_capture(sess, &sess->request_job.dst->vb2_buf,
+					       sess->request_job.dst->vb2_buf.index);
 		meson_amvdec_request_signal(sess, sess->request_job.dst);
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
@@ -439,6 +441,8 @@
 		sess->request_job.error = true;
 	}
 	meson_amvdec_write_dos(core, MREG_BUFFEROUT, 0);
+	meson_amvdec_shadow_to_capture(sess, &sess->request_job.dst->vb2_buf,
+				       sess->request_job.dst->vb2_buf.index);
 	meson_amvdec_request_signal(sess, sess->request_job.dst);
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
